```bash lucio command=execute show_source=false stdout=false stderr=false
# hidden block to ensure no files/directories used in the example below exist
rm -rf /tmp/cover.jpg /tmp/cover.jpg.json
rm -rf /tmp/audio.flac /tmp/audio.flac.json
rm -rf /tmp/o/
```

```bash lucio command=execute show_source=false stdout=false stderr=false
# hidden block to ensure a certain queue is playing
volumito playlist play "volumito test qobuz multiple albums 4 tracks"
```

## Download

> [!NOTE]
> In the examples below, wherever an explicit `-o` override is not present,
> the destination directory is `/tmp/o/`
> since it is defined in the configuration file used to generate this document.
>
> See Sections
> [Check Your Volumito Configuration File](#check-your-volumito-configuration-file)
> and [The Configuration File](#the-configuration-file) for details.

### Download Track

#### Download Track Albumart (Cover)

```bash lucio command=execute
volumito queue track albumart
```

```bash lucio command=execute
volumito queue track albumart -o /tmp/cover.jpg
```

#### Download Track Audio

```bash lucio command=execute
volumito queue track audio
```

```bash lucio command=execute
volumito queue track audio -o /tmp/audio.flac
```

### Download Queue

```bash lucio command=execute show_source=false stdout=false stderr=false
# hidden block to ensure no directory used in this section exist
rm -rf /tmp/o/
```

```bash lucio command=execute
volumito queue download
```

### Download Playlist

```bash lucio command=execute show_source=false stdout=false stderr=false
# hidden block to ensure no directory used in this section exist
rm -rf /tmp/o/
```

```bash lucio command=execute
volumito playlist download "volumito test qobuz multiple albums 4 tracks"
```

```bash lucio command=execute show_source=false stdout=false stderr=false
# hidden block to cleanup the files/directories used in the example above
rm -rf /tmp/cover.jpg /tmp/cover.jpg.json
rm -rf /tmp/audio.flac /tmp/audio.flac.json
rm -rf /tmp/o/
```
